Wait, I just realized something. Let me re-read the end of `punycode_decode`:

```c
*output_length = (size_t) out;
```

`out` is `punycode_uint` (uint32_t). `*output_length` is `size_t`. If `out` is, say, 63, then `*output_length = 63`. All `name_u32[0..62]` are written. Fine.

But what if `out` is 0? Then `*output_length = 0`. `_idn2_label_test(test_flags, name_u32, 0)` - reads 0 elements. Fine.

